## Part 2 — Runtime Selection (CLI vs MCP)

The agent picks its browser-driving channel before doing anything else, because
it determines cost and capability.

```
Does the runtime have filesystem access?  (Copilot agent mode / Claude Code / Cursor → YES)
│
├── YES → use @playwright/cli           # ~4x more token-efficient; snapshots/screenshots saved to disk
│         The agent reasons over files, not over a streamed accessibility tree.
│
└── NO  → use @playwright/mcp           # streams structured accessibility snapshots into context
          Required when the agent cannot read artifacts from disk.
```

**Primary path (Copilot in VS Code):** CLI-first.
**When deep, iterative page exploration of an unfamiliar UI is needed:** MCP is
acceptable for the Planner phase only, then hand back to CLI for generation.

Restricted capability profile for either channel:

```
core, navigation, interaction, snapshot, screenshot
# --isolated  (fresh, ephemeral profile per run — no leaked state)
# --allowed-origins <scheme://host of target_url>
# NEVER enable: evaluate / run_code_unsafe / file (unless target is fully trusted AND task requires it)
```

