## Part 3 — Phase Pipeline (The Orchestration Loop)

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Inputs: target_url + nl_scenario + optional auth] --> B[Part 5: Preflight gate]
    B -->|pass| C[Part 6: Establish session / storageState]
    B -->|fail| Z[STOP - report missing prerequisites]
    C --> D[Planner: explore LIVE app -> specs/plan.md]
    D --> E{Human checkpoint:\nplan matches observed behavior?}
    E -->|no| D
    E -->|yes| F[Generator: replay live -> tests/*.spec.ts]
    F --> G[Execute: npx playwright test]
    G --> H{All pass?}
    H -->|yes| I[Part 9: Stability gate --repeat-each]
    H -->|no| J[Healer: re-inspect live, repair, re-run]
    J --> K{Fixed within iteration cap?}
    K -->|yes| I
    K -->|no| Y[ESCALATE - human review, mark skipped, log reasoning]
    I -->|stable| L[Part 11: Evidence report]
    I -->|flaky| J
    L --> M[Done]
```

The three official agents map to phases as follows:
- **Planner** — explores the live app and writes a numbered Markdown plan to
  `specs/`. Writes **no code**. Needs a reachable, stable app (and a session for
  gated flows).
- **Generator** — reads one plan scenario (referenced **by number**, not name),
  replays it in a live browser, and writes a `.spec.ts` whose locators and
  assertions are derived from what it observed.
- **Healer** — runs the suite; on failure it replays the failing steps,
  distinguishes a real regression from a drifted locator, and repairs the test
  (or marks it skipped if the feature itself appears broken).

Bootstrap command (run once per repo, regenerate when Playwright updates):

```bash
npx playwright init-agents --loop=copilot   # or --loop=vscode | claude | opencode
```

