## Part 5 — Preflight Gate (Fail Fast, Report Explicitly)

Before any browser launches, verify and **report each line as PASS / FAIL**.
A single FAIL on a required item halts the run with an explicit reason.

```
[ ] Playwright >= 1.56 installed            (npx playwright --version)
[ ] Browser binaries present                (npx playwright install chromium)
[ ] VS Code >= 1.105 + Copilot agent mode   (required for the agentic loop)
[ ] Agent definitions exist                 (./.github/ or ./.claude/agents/ or ./agents/)
[ ] target_url is reachable and returns 2xx/3xx
[ ] target_url renders to a stable state    (no perpetual spinners on load)
[ ] If auth required: auth_context provided  (else gated steps are out of scope)
[ ] Channel selected per Part 2              (CLI vs MCP)
[ ] Capability + origin restrictions applied per Part 2
```

If a prerequisite is missing, the report states exactly which one and the exact
remediation command — it never proceeds on assumptions.

