## Part 13 — Known Limits (Stated Up Front)

- **Live app required.** The Planner cannot explore a URL that will not load or
  render to a stable state.
- **Auth is a prerequisite, not a feature.** Gated flows need a pre-established
  session; otherwise only public portions are covered.
- **AI selector choice is not infallible.** Even live-grounded, the agents can
  occasionally pick a sub-optimal locator — Part 11.3 surfaces every choice for
  human review precisely because of this.
- **Not for high-volume regression.** For large, stable matrices, run the
  generated specs as ordinary compiled tests in CI; the agentic loop is for
  authoring and healing, not bulk execution.
- **Stability gate is probabilistic.** `--repeat-each=10` reduces but cannot
  fully eliminate the chance of latent flake.

